### Executive Summary

A rule-loading protocol — encoded in `AGENTS.md` — was designed to require language models to discover, read, and cite domain-specific rules before responding to user prompts. The protocol is deliberately multi-step: the model must search an index, load matching files via tool calls, and declare what it loaded in a structured header.

The protocol was evaluated against {{ total_models }} frontier models. The results reveal a striking variance in compliance — from {{ "%.0f"|format(results[0].pass_rate * 100) if results else "100" }}% to {{ "%.0f"|format(results[-1].pass_rate * 100) if results else "17" }}% — across models that are otherwise considered capability peers.

