### For Eval Design

- **Widen capture hooks:** Don't only hook `read_file` — also capture bash calls that access the same paths.
- **Cumulative read tracking:** Track `read_file` calls across the entire conversation.
- **Manifest-based verification:** Compare Gate 3 citations against the rule-loader manifest.
- **Minimum 3 runs per fixture:** Single-run evaluation is insufficient for any model below 99%.

### Methodology Notes

Not all models followed the protocol on first exposure. Top-tier models (compliant tier, ≥98%) required no prompt iteration — they correctly executed the multi-step sequence on the first attempt. The partial and non-compliant tiers benefited from wording adjustments to the AGENTS.md bootstrap protocol, though even after iteration some models remain resistant to text-based intervention.

Some models exhibit behavior that is invariant to protocol wording changes: they shortcut the grounding sequence regardless of how the instructions are phrased. For these models, architectural interventions (retry loops, verification layers, simplified protocols) are more effective than prompt refinement.

